cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Meridia, please cite it as below.
title: "Meridia: synthetic countries for testing statistical methods"
abstract: >-
  Meridia generates synthetic countries from a seed: terrain, rivers,
  settlements, and a population of individual people with households,
  ages, incomes, employers, and health histories. Surveys and registers
  drawn from that population carry the flaws real collection produces.
  Because the complete population is retained, the error of any estimate
  is known exactly and stated uncertainty can be checked against true
  coverage.
type: software
authors:
